WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.791
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level one.

2
00:00:06.091 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:15.820
Unit twenty-three: Arts and Culture News. Today you will express opinions with -ing and -ed adjectives.

4
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.633
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.927
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.668
Arts.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:29.599
Arts means activities such as painting, music, dance and theatre.

8
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:32.345
The arts bring joy to every community.

9
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.451
Your turn. Say: Arts.

10
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.324
Arts.

11
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:41.177
Exhibition.

12
00:00:42.183 --> 00:00:45.216
Exhibition means a public display of works of art.

13
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.710
The exhibition showed paintings from five provinces.

14
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:51.772
Your turn. Say: Exhibition.

15
00:00:54.633 --> 00:00:55.774
Exhibition.

16
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:57.448
Review.

17
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:02.574
Review means an article giving an opinion about a book, show or film.

18
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:05.148
The review praised the dancers.

19
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.704
Your turn. Say: Review.

20
00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:12.405
Review.

21
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.232
Performance.

22
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:18.017
Performance means a show given in front of an audience.

23
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:20.895
The performance ended with loud applause.

24
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:24.182
Your turn. Say: Performance.

25
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.209
Performance.

26
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.835
Festival.

27
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:35.032
Festival means a public celebration with music, food or events.

28
00:01:35.617 --> 00:01:37.848
The water festival attracted millions.

29
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.033
Your turn. Say: Festival.

30
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:44.763
Festival.

31
00:01:45.517 --> 00:01:46.587
Heritage.

32
00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:51.173
Heritage means traditions and objects handed down from the past.

33
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:54.201
Heritage connects the present with history.

34
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:57.260
Your turn. Say: Heritage.

35
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.113
Heritage.

36
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:02.561
Critic.

37
00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.803
Critic means a person who judges art, books or films.

38
00:02:07.417 --> 00:02:09.695
The critic admired the stage design.

39
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:12.448
Your turn. Say: Critic.

40
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.115
Critic.

41
00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:17.828
Audience.

42
00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:22.302
Audience means the people who watch or listen to a performance.

43
00:02:22.917 --> 00:02:24.568
The audience stood and cheered.

44
00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:27.592
Your turn. Say: Audience.

45
00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:31.434
Audience.

46
00:02:32.233 --> 00:02:35.780
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:36.617 --> 00:02:42.427
Visal, a review says 'The performance was moving, and the audience was deeply moved.' Why -ing and -ed?

48
00:02:43.517 --> 00:02:54.726
-ing adjectives describe the thing that causes a feeling: a moving performance. -ed adjectives describe the person who feels it: moved, amazed, bored.

49
00:02:55.817 --> 00:02:57.654
So the critic can choose either?

50
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:07.233
Yes, but the meaning changes. An astonishing exhibition makes people astonished. Reviews use both to show opinion.

51
00:03:08.317 --> 00:03:11.175
Why is heritage so common in culture news?

52
00:03:12.283 --> 00:03:20.668
Because a festival or an exhibition can protect heritage, and critics help readers decide which events are worth visiting.

53
00:03:21.833 --> 00:03:23.183
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:27.433
Grammar focus: -ing and -ed adjectives in reviews.

55
00:03:27.733 --> 00:03:28.780
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:29.483 --> 00:03:31.100
The performance was moving.

57
00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:33.809
The audience was deeply moved.

58
00:03:34.717 --> 00:03:38.539
The exhibition was astonishing, and visitors were astonished.

59
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:45.772
Use -ing adjectives for the thing that causes a feeling (a boring film) and -ed adjectives for the person who feels it (I am bored).

60
00:03:46.517 --> 00:03:49.506
Be careful! Don't say: The show was bored.

61
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.222
Say: The show was boring.

62
00:03:53.522 --> 00:03:55.650
Use -ing for the thing causing the feeling.

63
00:03:56.433 --> 00:03:59.028
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:59.833 --> 00:04:01.357
A Night at the Festival.

65
00:04:01.657 --> 00:04:06.013
A cultural festival fills the city with colour, music and heritage.

66
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.136
One critic called the dance performance stunning and the costumes amazing.

67
00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:16.304
The audience was thrilled, and many visitors left the exhibition inspired.

68
00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:21.993
In her review, the critic explained why traditional arts remain relevant today.

69
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.336
Such events keep a nation's heritage alive.

70
00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:30.737
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:31.583 --> 00:04:33.142
The performance was blank.

72
00:04:33.442 --> 00:04:36.561
A, moving. B, moved. C, move.

73
00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.192
The answer is A: moving.

74
00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:45.291
The audience was blank by the music.

75
00:04:45.591 --> 00:04:48.792
A, amazed. B, amazing. C, amaze.

76
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:54.043
The answer is A: amazed.

77
00:04:55.183 --> 00:04:58.541
A person who judges art, books or films is a blank.

78
00:04:58.841 --> 00:05:02.495
A, critic. B, festival. C, heritage.

79
00:05:06.033 --> 00:05:07.580
The answer is A: critic.

80
00:05:08.717 --> 00:05:10.414
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:10.714 --> 00:05:15.749
A, I am boring in the show.. B, I am bored in the show.. C, The show is bored..

82
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:22.043
The answer is B: I am bored in the show..

83
00:05:23.183 --> 00:05:26.123
According to the reading, the critic called the costumes…

84
00:05:26.423 --> 00:05:29.763
A, amazing. B, amazed. C, dull.

85
00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.404
The answer is A: amazing.

86
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.914
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:43.063
What cultural event would you like to review?

88
00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:53.420
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:53.720 --> 00:06:11.204
I would like to review the traditional dance festival in my province. The costumes are stunning, and the music is moving. The audience always leaves delighted. In my review, I would explain how the performance protects heritage and why young people should attend.

90
00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.259
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:18.753
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and -ing and -ed adjectives in reviews.

92
00:06:19.053 --> 00:06:24.050
Today's value is appreciation of beauty. Learn to notice and value the beauty around you.

93
00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.537
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:27.837 --> 00:06:31.058
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

